\begin{subfigure}{0.48\linewidth}\centering\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/new_scuba.png}\caption{Our improved protocol}\end{subfigure}
\caption{Example clip from the UCF101-SCUBA-Sinusoid protocol for the class ``Skiing''. (a) The previous protocol leaves snow visible in the background. (b) Our protocol uses tight segmentation masks to eliminate the background.}
\label{fig:scuba}
\end{figure}
SCUBA replaces the background of a test video with Places365 images \citep{zhou2017places}, VQGAN-CLIP generated images \citep{crowson2022vqgan}, or sinusoidal stripe patterns while preserving the actor via a mask; SCUFO stacks a single frame of a SCUBA video to remove motion \citep{li2023mitigating}. The original UCF101 protocol uses THUMOS-14 \citep{THUMOS14} bounding boxes as masks, which lets background leak (Figure~\ref{fig:scuba}a). We use the boxes as grounding for initial proposals and refine them into tight actor masks with SAMTrack \citep{cheng2023segment}. Masks are generated automatically and then manually checked for every test video so that no residual background around the actor remains. No external attribute labels are required, and splits and class counts are unchanged from the prior design.

\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Setup}
We use a Video Swin Transformer Swin-T \citep{liu2022video} pretrained on Kinetics-400 \citep{carreira2017quo}, with 32 frames per clip at stride 2 and $224\times224$ resolution, random resized crop and horizontal flip. We use AdamW ($\beta_1{=}0.9$, $\beta_2{=}0.999$), weight decay 0.01, base learning rate $10^{-4}$ at batch size 64, 5 warmup epochs and a cosine schedule. We evaluate on HMDB51 \citep{kuehne2011hmdb} and UCF101 \citep{soomro2012ucf101}, on IID test sets and the OOD SCUBA and SCUFO sets, plus Confl-FG (a conflicting foreground inserted on sinusoid SCUBA), and on the rare-scene ARAS set. Metrics are Top-1 accuracy on SCUBA (higher is better, less background bias), on SCUFO (lower is better, less foreground/static bias), and \emph{contrasted accuracy}, where a prediction counts as correct only if the model is right on a SCUBA clip and wrong on its SCUFO counterpart, capturing background and foreground debiasing together. Baselines are Mixup, VideoMix, SDN, BE, ActorCutMix, FAME and StillMix. The overview does not report the values of $\omega_{adv},\omega_{ent},\omega_{gp}$, the number of runs or variance, so we report single numbers as given.

